{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793009477,"nonce":"+8gkIOATRJeLJis11vLruoS4ybE=","title":"Persist resumable Cloud Sync uploads and atomic workspace generations","message":"Parent plan: e003324b4983bd187aa32106d22f198e4ad218eebe4eea5edb10793ef31e4b1a\n\nExtend the Rust Worker/Workspace Durable Object with desktop snapshot import jobs, private R2 chunks/manifests and a stable workspace ID independent of compute. Reuse the repository-import route through a source-kind contract; do not require GitHub checkout for native uploads. Reserve account/workspace quota before accepting bytes, stream bounded multipart chunks outside DO memory, validate length/hash/ownership, resume/retry/cancel idempotently and garbage-collect abandoned parts. Publish a manifest generation atomically after all required data is durable; failed uploads retain the last valid generation. Return the copyable authorized app URL after publication, with compute readiness separate. Enforce auth and expiresAt on all operations. Prove concurrent uploads cannot overrun reservations or replace a newer generation. Prefer bounded authenticated transfer for the initial release; direct signed transfers require explicit proof of equivalent bounds.","files":null}]}